Looking at the four failures, none is a literal/empty-result problem (the pattern P1 already covers): sp0755 and sp0362 are **projection/filter-scope** errors ("which countries" → gold returns all entity columns; filter applied to the wrong table), sp0536 is a **duplicate-row/grain** error (8 rows vs 5 because enrolment rows were not deduplicated), sp0894 is an **anti-join scope** error that yields 0 rows and never gets repaired. So this candidate targets semantics of *what* to select / which rows count, plus giving the repair loop a chance on suspicious empty results.

Two independent edits: (1) prompt rules for entity-wide projections, filtering on the entity that owns the text, one-row-per-entity grain, and symmetric relationship anti-joins; (2) harness-side duplicate-row detection + repair trigger on empty results even when probes find nothing, with row-grain evidence fed back.

